TITLE:: MENoteRange
summary:: Public interface of MusicEngine.
categories:: MusicEngine Library
related:: Classes/MERange, Classes/MENote, Classes/MERegister, Reference/RangeSymbols

DESCRIPTION::
MENoteRange is MusicEngine's primary tool for accessing collections of MENote objects.


CLASSMETHODS::

copymethod:: MERange, *new

METHOD:: newFromName
Allows the creation of a new MENoteRange from a sequence of note names.

ARGUMENT:: ... names
Sequence of note names as strings. Note names must contain an uppercase letter (EMPhASIS::A-G::), 0 to 5 accidentals and an octave number (-1 to 9). (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C4", "Eb4", "G#4"::, etc.).

ARGUMENT:: kwargs
Optional keyword arguments for attaching user data to each MENote object. Each value must be an array of the same length as the number of notes provided (i.e. the size of CODE::args::). The keys become identifiers stored in each MENote's internal data dictionary. If the value arrays are not the same size as EMPHASIS::notes::, the method will throw an Error.

NOTE::
The special keyword CODE::\degrees:: is used to attach interval information to each note. The value must be an array of interval symbols (e.g.: CODE::[\P1, \M3, \P5, ...]::). Internally each symbol is used to instantiate a MEInterval object, which is then assigned to the CODE::degree:: property of the corresponding MENote.
All other keyword arguments are stored directly (without conversion) in each MENote's data dictionary.
::

returns:: A new MENoteRange object.

NOTE::
If any of the note names is not valid, or if the length of one of the value arrays, passed as kwarg, does not match the number of note names, the method will throw an Error.
::

CODE::
(
// Take the A train
r = MENoteRange.newFromName(
	"G4", "E5", "G4", "C5", "E5", "G#4", "A4", "Bb4", "B4", "E5", "G4", "F#4", "F4", "C#5", "C5", "E4",
	degrees:  [\P5, \M3, \P5, \P1, \M3, \A5, \M6, \m7, \M7, \M3, \P5, \A4, \P4, \A1, \P1, \M3],
	dur:      [4.5, 1.5, 1, 1, 0.5, 7.5, 5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 4]
);

// Create a pattern
t = TempoClock.new(120/60);
Pbind(
	\midinote, r.asPseq(\midi, 1, 0),
	\dur, r.asPseq(\dur, 1, 0)
).play(t);
)

// Degree data
r[0].degree;
r[0].number;
r[0].quality;
// etc.
::


INSTANCEMETHODS::


SUBSECTION:: Data retrieval

copymethod:: MERange, -notes

METHOD:: midi
Returns an array of MIDI values.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].midi;
::


METHOD:: freq
Returns an array with frequency values;

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].freq;
::


METHOD:: names
Returns an array of note names in scientific notation (EMPHASIS::A::-EMPHASIS::G::). The argument EMPHASIS::charSet:: should be of type Symbol, and allows the user to choose between different characters sets to represent the accidental signs. The argument EMPHASIS::withOctave:: is a Boolean flag that determines whether an octave number should be appended to the string.

NOTE:: For the argument EMPHASIS::charSet::, the following values are accepted:
LIST::
## CODE::\ascii:: for ASCII characters (# and b),
## CODE::\unic:: for Unicode characters (𝄪, ♯, ♭ and 𝄫),
## CODE::\m21:: for a format compatible with the Python's module music21 (# and -).
::
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].names;
r[20..25].names(charSet: \unic);    // For Unicode characters
r[20..25].names(withOctave: false); // Names with no octave number
::


METHOD:: sol
Similar to CODE::names::, but uses the fixed-do Solfège naming convention.

NOTE:: The argument EMPHASIS::charSet:: only accepts the following values:
LIST::
## CODE::\ascii:: for ASCII characters (# and b),
## CODE::\unic:: for Unicode characters (𝄪, ♯, ♭ and 𝄫),
## CODE::\m21:: for a format compatible with the Python's module music21 (# and -).
::
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].sol;
r[20..25].sol(charSet: \unic);    // For Unicode characters
r[20..25].sol(withOctave: false); // Names with no octave number
::


METHOD:: degrees
Returns an array of interval symbols.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].degrees;
::


METHOD:: symbol
Returns a verbose range symbol (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"F#m3P5m7"::). If EMPHASIS::withRoot:: is set to CODE::true::, the root name will be appended at the start.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.symbol;        // F#m3P5m7
r.symbol(false); // m3P5m7
::


METHOD:: alias
Returns the alias of the range symbol. If no alias was used CODE::nil:: is returned. If EMPHASIS::withRoot:: is set to CODE::true::, the root name will be appended at the start.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.alias;        // F#-7
r.alias(false); // -7
::


METHOD:: root
Returns the root note of the range. If EMPHASIS::offset:: is set to CODE::true:: a MIDI offset will be returned instead of a string.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.root;       // F#
r.root(true); // 6
::


METHOD:: intervals
Returns an array with the intervals that make up the range. If EMPHASIS::asSymbol:: is set to CODE::true::, an array of interval symbol is returned, otherwise it returns an array with a float representation of the intervals.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.intervals;        // [P1, m3, P5, m7]
r.intervals(false); // [1.2, 3.1, 5.2, 7.1]
::


METHOD:: asPseq
Returns data as Pseq objects (with the exception of degrees and names). EMPHASIS::what:: takes a symbol indicating the data to be returned (CODE::\midi::, CODE::\freq::, etc.); the sequence is repeated EMPHASIS::rep:: number of times, starting from EMPHASIS::off:: position.

CODE::
(
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

p = r[20..30];
p.setValue(\dur, 0.5); // Assigns duration values
p.setValue(\leg, 0.2); // Assigns articulation values

Pbind(
	\midinote, p.asPseq(\midi, 1, 0),
	\legato,   p.asPseq(\leg, 1, 0),
	\dur,      p.asPseq(\dur, 1, 0)
).play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Trimming methods


METHOD:: trimO
Returns all MENote with octave numbers MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::fromOctave:: and MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::toOctave::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.trimO(4, 5); // Returns items from octaves 4 and 5
::


METHOD:: trimM
Returns all MENote with MIDI values MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::fromMIDI:: and MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::toMIDI::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.trimM(48, 72); // Range between MIDI notes 48 and 72
::


METHOD:: trimF
Returns all MENote with frequency values MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::fromFreq:: and MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::toFreq::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.trimF(500, 1000); // Range between 500Hz and 1000Hz
::


METHOD:: trimD
Returns all MENote starting from the first occurrence of EMPHASIS::fromDegree::, to the last occurrence of EMPHASIS::toDegree::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.trimD(\P1, \P5); // From the first P1 found, to the last P5 found
::


METHOD:: trimN
Returns all MENote starting from the first instance of EMPHASIS::fromName::, searching upwards from the bottom, to the last occurrence of EMPHASIS::toName::, searching downwards from the top.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.trimN("F#", "C#"); // From the first F# found, to the last C# found
::


METHOD:: bTrimO
Trims the bottom of the range by returning all MENote objects with octave numbers MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::fromOctave::. If EMPHASIS::fromOctave:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.bTrimO(7); // Returns octaves 7, 8 and 9
::


METHOD:: bTrimM
Trims the bottom of the range by returning all MENote objects with MIDI values MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::fromMIDI::. If EMPHASIS::fromMIDI:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.bTrimM(100); // From MIDI value 100
c[0].midi;         // 100
::


METHOD:: bTrimF
Trims the bottom of the range by returning all MENote objects with frequency values MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::fromFreq::. If EMPHASIS::fromFreq:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.bTrimF(2000); // From 2000Hz
c[0].freq;          // Closest at 2217.46Hz
::


METHOD:: bTrimD
Trims the bottom of the range by starting the sequence at the first instance of a MENote that matches EMPHASIS::fromDegree::. If EMPHASIS::fromDegree:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.bTrimD(\m3); // Starts from A-1:m3
::


METHOD:: bTrimN
Trims the bottom of the range by starting the sequence at the first instance of a MENote that matches EMPHASIS::fromName::. If EMPHASIS::fromName:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.bTrimN("A"); // Starts from A-1:m3
::


METHOD:: tTrimO
Trims the top of the range by returning all MENote objects with octave numbers MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::toOctave::. If EMPHASIS::toOctave:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.tTrimO(4); // Ends with the last note with octave 4
::


METHOD:: tTrimM
Trims the top of the range by returning all MENote objects with MIDI values MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::toMIDI::. If EMPHASIS::toMIDI:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.tTrimM(48);
::


METHOD:: tTrimF
Trims the top of the range by returning all MENote objects with frequency values MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::toFreq::. If EMPHASIS::toFreq:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.tTrimF(100);
::


METHOD:: tTrimD
Trims the top of the range by ending the sequence at the last instance of a MENote that matches EMPHASIS::toDegree::. If EMPHASIS::toDegree:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.tTrimD(\m3);
::


METHOD:: tTrimN
Trims the top of the range by ending the sequence at the last instance of a MENote that matches EMPHASIS::toName::. If EMPHASIS::toName:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.tTrimN("A");
::


METHOD:: ><
Shorthand from all double-ended trimming methods. The argument EMPHASIS::limits:: accepts an array of size 2, where both values are of the same type. Numeric values should be sorted from smallest to greatest.  If EMPHASIS::limits:: are not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE::
Depending on the input >< will call on different methods:
::

table::
 ## String SOFT::(without octave)::                || CODE::trimN(fromName, toName)::
 ## Symbol                                         || CODE::trimD(fromDegree, toDegree)::
 ## Integer MATH::\ge -1:: AND MATH::\le 9::       || CODE::trimO(fromOctave, toOctave)::
 ## Integer MATH::\ge 12:: AND MATH::\le 127::     || CODE::trimM(fromMIDI, toMIDI)::
 ## Float MATH::\ge 20.0:: AND MATH::\le 20000.0:: || CODE::trimF(fromFreq, toFreq)::
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

// Trims by frequency, then by degree and then by note name
r >< [500.0,10000.0] >< [\P1,\P1] >< ["A","E"];

// Same as:
r.trimF(500.0, 10000.0).trimD(\P1, \P1).trimN("A", "E");
::


METHOD:: |>
Shorthand for all bottom trimming methods. If EMPHASIS::limit:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE::
Depending on the input |> will call on different methods:
::

table::
 ## String SOFT::(without octave)::                || CODE::bTrimN(fromName)::
 ## Symbol                                         || CODE::bTrimD(fromDegree)::
 ## Integer MATH::\ge -1:: AND MATH::\le 9::       || CODE::bTrimO(fromOctave)::
 ## Integer MATH::\ge 12:: AND MATH::\le 127::     || CODE::bTrimM(fromMIDI)::
 ## Float MATH::\ge 20.0:: AND MATH::\le 20000.0:: || CODE::bTrimF(fromFreq)::
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

// Trims the bottom by frequency, then by degree and then by note name
r |> 1000.0 |> \P1 |> "A";

// Same as:
r.bTrimF(1000.0).bTrimD(\P1).bTrimN("A");
::


METHOD:: <|
Shorthand for all top trimming methods. If EMPHASIS::limit:: is not valid, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE::
Depending on the input <| will call on different methods:
::

table::
 ## String SOFT::(without octave)::                || CODE::tTrimN(toName)::
 ## Symbol                                         || CODE::tTrimD(toDegree)::
 ## Integer MATH::\ge -1:: AND MATH::\le 9::       || CODE::tTrimO(toOctave)::
 ## Integer MATH::\ge 12:: AND MATH::\le 127::     || CODE::tTrimM(toMIDI)::
 ## Float MATH::\ge 20.0:: AND MATH::\le 20000.0:: || CODE::tTrimF(toFreq)::
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

// Trims by frequency, then by degree and then by note name
r <| 100.0 <| \P1 <| "E";

// Same as:
r.tTrimF(100.0).tTrimD(\P1).tTrimN("E");
::


SUBSECTION:: Filtering methods


METHOD:: filterD
Returns a MENoteRange with all instances of MENote objects with matching EMPHASIS::degrees:: removed.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.filterD(\P1, \P5); // Removes all P1 and P5 notes
::

METHOD:: filterN
Returns a MENoteRange with all instances of MENote objects with matching EMPHASIS::names:: removed.

NOTE::
Note names may include octave numbers or not. Names with no octave are not unique, so all items with matching names will be removed. Names with octave, on the other hand, are unique and allow for the removal of specific items.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

a = r.filterN("F#", "C#"); // Removes all F# and C# notes

// Has the same effects as:
b = r.filterD(\P1, \P5);
a == b; // true

r.filterN("F#4", "C#5"); // Only two notes are removed
::


METHOD:: |
Shorthand for methods CODE::filterD:: and CODE::filterN::. Only one EMPHASIS::item:: allowed per call.

NOTE::
Depending on the input | will call on different methods:
::

table::
 ## String SOFT::(with or without octave):: || CODE::filterN(... names)::
 ## Symbol                                  || CODE::filterD(... degrees)::
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

a = r | \P1 | "C#" | "E4"; // Removes all P1 notes, all C# notes and E4

// Same as:
b = r.filterD(\P1).filterN("C#").filterN("E4");
a == b; // true
::


METHOD:: span
Returns a MENoteRange with MENotes filtered such that notes with degrees under the octave are separated from those with degrees above. This method can only be applied to ranges with symbols that contain degrees larger than a seventh (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"F#-13"::). If the range does not contain degrees over the seventh, the original range will be returned without modification. This method creates a pattern that spans two octaves before repeating.

NOTE::
The sequence may start from any range note.
::

WARNING::
This method should not be used after other filtering methods have been applied, or its behaviour might become unpredictable.
::

CODE::
// Instead of having all the notes wrapped in an octave, as such:
// P1 - M9 - m3 - P11 - P5 - M13 - m7
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-13");
c = r >< [4, 8] |> \P1;

// The notes are ordered according to their distance to P1:
// P1 - m3 - P5 - m7 - M9 - P11 - M13
c.span

// Starting from M9
c = r >< [4, 8] |> \M9;
c.span;

// A single interval over the octave;
r = MENoteRange.new("F#P11");

c = r >< [4, 8] |> \P1;
c.span

// Starting from P11
c = r >< [4, 8] |> \P11;
c.span

// Using span on a range without degrees over the seventh
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.span; // Nothing has changed
c == r;     // true
::


SUBSECTION:: User-assigned data


METHOD:: setValue
Sets single EMPHASIS::value:: to all data dictionaries, and associates them to a EMPHASIS::key::.

NOTE::
If EMPHASIS::inplace:: is set to CODE::false::, the method returns a copy of the range. This prevents data contamination.
::

CODE::
a = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

// Sets value 1 to key \dur in all dictionaries
c = a[20..25].setValue(\dur, 1, inplace: true);

// Returns array with all values associated with \dur
c.getValues(\dur);

// We get data contamination
a.getValues(\dur); // [..., nil, 1, ..., 1, nil, ...]


// Alternativelly, with inplace set to false:
b = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = b[20..25].setValue(\dur, 1, inplace: false);
c.getValues(\dur);

// No contamination
b.getValues(\dur); // ERROR: Key 'dur' is not defined.
::


METHOD:: setValues
Sets a EMPHASIS::sequence:: of values to the data dictionaries, by position, and associates them to a EMPHASIS::key::. EMPHASIS::sequence:: should be of the size of range.

NOTE::
If EMPHASIS::inplace:: is set to CODE::false::, the method returns a copy of the range. This prevents data contamination.
::

CODE::
(
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

r = r[20..30];
r.size; // 11

// Set values
a = Array.interpolation(r.size, 0.1, 1.0);
r.setValues(\amp, a);
r.setValues(\dur, [0.5, 1, 0.5, 1, 0.5, 1, 0.5, 1, 0.5, 1, 0.5]);

// Check values
r.getValues(\amp).postln;
r.getValues(\dur).postln;
)

(
Pbind(
	\freq, r.asPseq(\freq, 1, 0),
	\amp,  r.asPseq(\amp, 1, 0),
	\dur,  r.asPseq(\dur, 1, 0)
).play;
)
::


METHOD:: setFunc
Sets a values to all data dictionaries by evaluating a EMPHASIS::function:: and associates them to a EMPHASIS::key::.

NOTE::
If EMPHASIS::inplace:: is set to CODE::false::, the method returns a copy of the range. This prevents data contamination.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

r = r[20..30];

// Set values
r.setFunc(\dur, { rrand(0.125, 2.0) });

// Check values
r.getValues(\dur);

(
Pbind(
	\freq, r.asPseq(\freq, 1, 0),
	\dur,  r.asPseq(\dur, 1, 0)
).play;
)
::


METHOD:: getValues
Returns an array with all the values associated with a given EMPHASIS::key::. If the EMPHASIS::key:: does not exist an Error is thrown.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r = r[20..30];

r.setValue(\amp, 1);

r.getValues(\amp); // Returns array of values
r.getValues(\dur); // ERROR: Key 'dur' is not defined.
::


METHOD:: getKeys
Returns a set with all the different keys stored in the dictionaries.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r = r[20..30];

r.setValue(\amp, 0.5);
r.setValue(\dur, 1);
r.setValue(\leg, 0.2);

r.getKeys; // Set[leg, dur, amp]
::


METHOD:: clearValues
Clears all values associated with a EMPHASIS::key::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r = r[20..30];

r.setValue(\dur, 0.5);

r.getValues(\dur);   // [0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5]
r.clearValues(\dur); // Clears values associated to \dur
r.getValues(\dur);   // ERROR: Key 'dur' is not defined.
::


METHOD:: clearDict
Clears all values stored in the data dictionaries.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r = r[20..30];

r.setValue(\amp, 0.5);
r.setValue(\dur, 1);

r.getKeys;   // Set[amp, dur]
r.clearDict; // Clears all data
r.getKeys;   // Set[]
::


SUBSECTION:: Range transposition


METHOD:: >>
Transposes all notes in the range upward by EMPHASIS::interval::, updating MIDI values, frequencies and note names (with correct spelling).
Successive calls produces new transposed copies until either the MIDI value exceeds 127 or at least one note has more than 5 accidentals. At that point, the method keeps returning the last valid transposition.

NOTE::
EMPHASIS::interval:: may be expressed using an integer MATH::\ge 0::, or a symbol describing an interval (e.g.: CODE::\M2::). Integer values default to specific symbols as decribed in the section LINK::Classes/MENote#Note transposition::.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

c = r >< [4, 6] |> \P1;

(
Routine({
	var syn;

	3.do {
		c.do { |n|
			n.name.postln;
			syn = Synth(\default, [\freq, n.freq, \gate, 1]);
			0.5.wait;
			syn.set(\gate, 0);
		};
		c = c >> \M2; // Transpose M2 up
		"".postln;
	};
	syn.release(2);
}).play;
)
::


METHOD:: <<
Transposes all notes in the range downward by EMPHASIS::interval::, updating MIDI values, frequencies and note names (with correct spelling).
Successive calls produces new transposed copies until either the MIDI value exceeds 0 or at least one note has more than 5 accidentals. At that point, the method keeps returning the last valid transposition.

NOTE::
EMPHASIS::interval:: may be expressed using an integer MATH::\ge 0::, or a symbol describing an interval (e.g.: CODE::\M2::). Integer values default to specific symbols as decribed in the section LINK::Classes/MENote#Note transposition::.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

c = r >< [4, 6] |> \P1;

(
Routine({
	var syn;

	3.do {
		c.do { |n|
			n.name.postln;
			syn = Synth(\default, [\freq, n.freq, \gate, 1]);
			0.5.wait;
			syn.set(\gate, 0);
		};
		c = c << 3; // Transpose m3 down
		"".postln;
	};
	syn.release(2);
}).play;
)
::
